<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav Aug copper output rises.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav Aug copper output rises.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV NON-FERROUS ORES	Aug 96    July 96   June 96</p>
<p> copper (thousand tonnes)	1,807	1,619	 1,737</p>
<p> lead-zinc				81	   77	    58</p>
<p> bauxite				  60	   15	    --</p>
<p>NON-FERROUS METAL PRODUCTION</p>
<p> electrolytic copper (tonnes) 11,368     11,927	 7,459</p>
<p> refined lead			3,440	3,140	 3,527</p>
<p> zinc				  3,205	2,660	 1,287</p>
<p> aluminium ingots		  3,769	4,122	 1,853</p>
<p> refined silver (kilos)	  7,083	5,292	 4,112</p>
<p>-- Gordana Filipovic, Belgrade newsroom, +381 11 222 4254</p>
</text>
